  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/air_rings_tests.rs`: `ring_plan()` returns `&'static (Region, Region, AirPlan)` from a `std::sync::LazyLock` (the style of `lift_tests.rs:37`). The old body is now `compute_ring_plan()`.\n- The three tests and the ignored probe `probe_air_hops` use the same plan. The binary computes the plan one time.\n- `every_air_ring_pass_stays_in_the_centre_area` passes `ring` in place of `&ring` to `boundary_dist`, because `ring` is a reference now. The asserts and their values do not change.\n- No change to `air_rings.rs` or to other tests. The binary is not split.\n\n## Readings\n\nCommand: `cargo test -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib air_rings::tests:: -- --test-threads=6` (debug, this machine). The \"finished in\" line:\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6 threads (gate form) | 8.56 s, 8.62 s, 8.47 s | 8.51 s, 8.34 s, 8.50 s |\n| 1 thread (extra reading) | 22.53 s | 8.51 s |\n| Plan computations in one run | 3 (6.7 s each) | 1 (6.5 s) |\n\n- `--report-time` is an unstable libtest flag. The table gives the totals.\n- With 6 threads, the three plans ran in parallel before. Thus the wall time stays the same. The change removes about 13 s of CPU work for each run of the lib binary. This CPU time is free for the other tests of `motion suites: lib`.\n- `#[test]` count of the file: 5 before, 5 after (1 ignored, the same one).\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p camcraft-motion --lib --profile test -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `a_ring_round_an_island_is_cut_from_the_air_within_budget`\n- `every_air_ring_pass_stays_in_the_centre_area`\n- `the_air_entry_disc_is_clear_of_the_stock`\n\nAll three are green.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The whole `motion` lib binary and the other motion test binaries. Only the `air_rings::tests::` filter ran.\n- The ignored probe `probe_air_hops`. It compiles. It did not run.\n- No heavy lane. The change is test code only.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3515\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
